 @theramatube  It's just as easy as going to take a piss.Just open Adrenaline -> performance tab-> fine tuning -> Gpu manual fine tuning, and on your left side you have options to tune clockspeed and voltage for the gpu.
Enable the small slider to open up the controls for adjustment. Once you've done it, enable the slider for advanced controls.Now the bottom slider of the Gpu finetuning controls propably says 1150mV, just pull that slider or enter your target number in the box to the left and press enter, then check "use changes" on top right corner. I think a stable undervolt for you to start would be around 1070mV. 
If everything is stable both idle and under load, pull back to 1060mV, hit apply and check for stability again, and repeat the process until you get a systemcrash or Radeon Wattman has been reset.So if you get a crash at 1000mV, I would set it to 1020mV or even 1030mV to ensure stability . You cannot break anything by undervolting, but don't do the base tests while downloading/installing updates and so on.

